  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "audxvBP0JHVFgqFJcHVbXuxjNyY=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:17.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "When you define an operation, you mark which scope it writes to. Codegen turns that into a typed action creator that passes the scope through to `createAction` automatically:\n\n```ts\n// generated creators.ts\nexport const setCursor = (input: SetCursorInput) =>\n  createAction<SetCursorAction>(\n    \"SET_CURSOR\",\n    { ...input },\n    undefined,       // deprecated attachments slot, retained for arity\n    SetCursorInputSchema,\n    \"local\",         // \u2190 scope, bound at generation time\n  );\n```\n\nThe scope is the **fifth positional argument** of `createAction`, and in source it is declared `scope: Action[\"scope\"] = \"global\"` (`packages/shared/document-model/actions.ts`). That default is the whole reason not to hand-roll the call: a forgotten fifth argument does not fail to compile and does not throw \u2014 it quietly routes a local-scope action into the global log, where it syncs to every peer. A per-user cursor position becomes shared state, and you find out from a collaborator, not from a test.\n\nThe generated creator also wires in the Zod input validator (fourth argument), so bypassing it loses input validation as well as scope binding. `createAction` additionally stamps `id: generateId()` and `timestampUtcMs` \u2014 which is exactly why those values are minted here, at dispatch time, and not inside the reducer.\n\nAlways import the creator. In a versioned project the generated creators live per-module under `v<n>/gen/<module>/creators.ts`, but the supported surface is the model's top-level barrel, which re-exports them as `actions.<actionName>`.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/02-Learn/08-deep-dives/01-reducers-in-depth.mdx, confirmed against packages/shared/document-model/actions.ts (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:17.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:17.000Z"
    }
  },
